-- title:
--   Trivial twist: σ=1 unipotent cell is untwisted
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $\alpha,\beta$ real numbers, $\Phi_1,\Phi_2$ subsets of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, $\nu_{Z_K}$ a measure on the idele units for a given measurable structure, $\Omega_K$ a subset of the idele units, $D$ a Galois descent datum for $K/K$ (a homomorphism from $K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}K$ to ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_K$, compatible with $K\to\mathbb{A}_K$ and continuous), `hgen` the hypothesis that every $\tau:K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}K$ lies in the subgroup generated by $1$, $\xi$ a homomorphism from the full group of idele units to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, and $\varphi:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathbb{C}$. Then for every real $R$ the following two iterated integrals coincide: in both, $x$ runs over `canonicalTruncationDomain K α β` against the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar`, and $z$ runs over $\Omega_K$ against $\nu_{Z_K}$, the inner integrand being $\xi(z)$ times a difference. On the left the first term is $\sum_{\delta}^{\mathrm{f}}\varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(z\cdot x)\bigr)$, over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ whose `normClassMap hgen` image of the $1$-twisted conjugacy class of $\delta$ is the conjugacy class of some $\gamma$ of unipotent type (not of central type, with characteristic polynomial $(X-a)^2$), where $\delta$ is viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, $z$ as the central scalar matrix, and $\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}$ is the map induced by $D.\mathrm{act}(1)$; on the right it is `adelicKernelUnipotentPart K φ x (z·x)`, that is $\sum_{\gamma}^{\mathrm{f}}\varphi(x^{-1}\gamma\, z x)$ over $\gamma$ of unipotent type. The subtracted term is, on both sides, the indicator of $\{g:\exp R<\mathrm{ht}_{\mathbb{A}}(g)\}$ at $z\cdot x$ times a constant term: the integral over $t\in\mathbb{A}_K$, against the normalised restriction of adelic additive Haar measure to `adelicBox` (the $\nu$-component of the `productionPinsOf` data, identical for both sides), of the value at $y=u(t)\cdot(z\cdot x)$, $u(t)=\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, of $y\mapsto\sum^{\mathrm{f}}\varphi(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(y))$ over upper-triangular $\delta$ with $N_{K/K}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11})=1$ on the left, and of $y\mapsto\sum^{\mathrm{f}}\varphi(x^{-1}\gamma\,y)$ over upper-triangular $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}=1$ on the right. The two sides use the pins built from $\Phi_1$ with level family $M\mapsto\mathrm{levelOne}(M)\sqcap\mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, respectively from $\Phi_2$ with $M\mapsto\mathrm{principalLevel}(M)\sqcap\mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, and the Hecke generators `heckeGen`.
--
--   This is the degenerate case of the comparison of twisted and untwisted unipotent contributions in the trace formula: for the trivial cyclic extension $K/K$ with generator $\sigma=1$, the $\sigma$-twisted unipotent cell, together with its truncation by the unipotent constant term, coincides with the untwisted unipotent part of the kernel and its truncation. It is used in [`AutomorphicForm.exists_tendsto_setIntegral_unipotentCell_sub_affine_atTop_of_isUnitFactorization`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_tendsto_setIntegral_unipotentCell_sub_affine_atTop_of_isUnitFactorization).
